Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||09-22-2000||07:38 AM||||amazingly enough, my 2.8 to 3.1 cost almost exactly what a 3.1 crate would have cost ($1600) advantage being that you don't have to worry about switching starter sides or anything. But I won't know how she pulls for a while longer, I've still gotta get a bunch more parts and extra stuff I just want to do befor she's together agian.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||09-22-2000||05:24 PM||||You can get ported heads from Norris racing for about $1000. Go into special projects and then into the 60-degree performance stuff. He sells them for 3.4 engines but the 3.4 and H.O. 2.8 heads are the same. <A HREF="http://www.norrisracingtech.com/home.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.norrisracingtech.com/home.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||HYPTNOTiSE||09-24-2000||02:45 AM||||I have comp cams roller rockers, springs, and retainers, I have modded Si stainless valves, New hardened bronze guides, new seats, i had a radius valve job done, and a full port and polish job done to my heads, and the total cost was about $1500.  <P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
